From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: ControlTemplate, ContentPresenter, TemplateBinding -- controls drawn by templates

Controls of programs are drawn by templates; there were none. ControlTemplate keeps its content as the markup it was read from and makes it again for each control it is applied to (a control's Template, from a style or its own value, is applied when it is first laid out; its OnApplyTemplate then runs -- an application's control finds its parts with GetTemplateChild there); {TemplateBinding X} sets a template element's member from the control's X and keeps it following; ContentPresenter shows the control's Content (bound to it unless given one), with the controls' text, border, background and padding members. A templated control draws nothing itself: its template does. Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT); the implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
